// A member call on a TYPE-PARAMETER receiver whose only instantiation carries the property as
// a closure FIELD, with NO free `self`-function of that name anywhere in the program.
// `vl check` returns 1 — with an EMPTY message: `[ERROR]:` followed by the caret line and no
// sentence at all.
//
// THE ABLATION IS ONE LINE, and it is the one nobody would write: add a free
// `function tag(self: Circle)` for a type this program never instantiates the generic at, and
// the identical program compiles and prints `fld`. That is D1002's own witness, which is why
// the shape looked covered — every fixture for the field-dispatch family carries a
// `self`-function, because the family is ABOUT the precedence between the two. With no
// `self`-function there is no precedence question, and that is the case that refuses.
//
// Two things to grade here, not one: the program must compile, and a refusal that survives
// for a DESIGN reason must still carry a sentence. See D1221.
// Should print fld.
type Boxed = { tag: () => string }

function describe<T>(x: T): string { x.tag() }

const b: Boxed = { tag: () => "fld" }
print(describe(b))
